@startuml SD-10_Explorer_ShiftTurn
title SD-10 · Explorer — one turn of a shift, with segment grading

actor Explorer
participant "Explorer app" as App
participant "Play" as Play
participant "Result stream" as RS
database "PostgreSQL" as DB
queue "Redis" as R
participant "AI orchestration" as AI
participant "Model gateway" as GW

Explorer -> App : Act, say, choose, ask a hint, or let time run out
App -> App : Compute provisional state with game-core
App -> Play : Submit turn with turn id
Play -> DB : Lock run, append turn event in one transaction
alt turn id already recorded
  DB --> Play : Existing result
else new turn
  Play -> R : Enqueue shift-turn job
end
Play --> App : Accepted, job id
App --> Explorer : Show "saved, assessing"

R -> AI : Take job
AI -> DB : Load run events
AI -> AI : Fold events with game-core, find pending request
opt engine needs a judgement or a scene
  AI -> GW : Narrate scene / answer yes-no question (de-identified)
  GW --> AI : Text with model, prompt version, cost, latency
end
AI -> DB : Append result events with provenance
AI -> R : Publish turn result
R --> RS : Turn result event
RS --> App : Push event
App --> Explorer : Show next beat

opt a segment closed
  AI -> GW : Grade segment against checklist (judge seats)
  GW --> AI : Checklist marks with quotations
  alt enough judges
    AI -> DB : Append grading event
  else too few judges
    AI -> DB : Keep answer, mark pending
    AI -> R : Publish provider delay
    R --> RS : Provider delay event
    RS --> App : Show wait message
  end
end
@enduml
